it is the late 13th century and the  small island of Tsushima is reeling from  an assault by the mongol empire with  most of its samurai defeated and the  once serene land now ravaged by flames  all hope the Tsushima seems lost  however samurai warrior jin Sakai  survived and has vowed to retake the  island and so the stage is set for ps4  exclusive ghosts of Tsushima a stunning  open-world samurai adventure and the  first game in six years from Sly Cooper  and infamous creators sucker punch  as he roams this beautiful island under  siege jin will discover enemy camps and  strongholds filled with deadly Mongol  warriors mastery of your katana is  paramount for face-to-face  confrontations combat is swift precise  and brutal no lengthy combo strings here  rather you engage in a series of tense  one-on-one standoffs where successfully  anticipating your rivals next move ends  their life with a single flash of your  blade some enemies will try to attack  from range so it's also possible to  quickly switch to a bow and land a  faithful arrow before they do the same  to you contributing to this elegant yet  complex juggling act is the ability to  switch stances depending on the weapon  and enemy wields you can switch to a  different stance that's better equipped  at parrying a specific type of attack  however as Jean is forced to adapt in  order to fight back he will also begin  to learn new dishonorable skills as he  transitions into the titular ghost  utilizing those skills Jin can become an  unseen antagonist using stealthy  movements disruptive gadgetry and a mix  of ranged and close-quarters  assassination techniques to thin the  ranks and generally strike fear into the  mongols by lurking in the shadows and  deploying tricky items like wind chimes  and firecrackers you can lure enemies  away from their cohorts and deliver a  swift silent kill if you're detected  hope is not lost throwing down a smoke  bomb gives you the opportunity to escape  but it can also disorient a 2-fold  sufficiently to create an opening for a  backstab it's not guaranteed though  especially if you're up against tougher  armored opposition fortunately you've  also got kunai daggers up your sleeve  take out enough troops to prove your  credentials as a one-man army as some  enemies may actually drop their weapons  out of fear and pray for mercy whether  you decide to grant them that mercy is  another matter entirely  [Music]  the final crucial element in ghosts of  Tsushima is customization the items you  dressed in in aren't just for show  although they can be dyed all manner of  shades and patterns they also provide  combat and exploration advantages  collectible amamori charms can be  equipped to various slots and are  designed to enhance and complement your  play style of choice turn the tide of a  seemingly unstoppable Mongol invasion  when ghosts of Tsushima releases  exclusively on PlayStation for July 17  [Music]
 

